{"title":"25","section":"636","heading":"Omitted","lead":"","tree":[],"notes":[{"topic":"editorialNotes","text":"Editorial Notes"},{"topic":"codification","text":"Codification Section, act Apr. 19, 1950, ch. 92, § 6, 64 Stat. 46, which related to the adoption of a constitution by the Navajo Tribe, was omitted from the Code as being of special and not general application."}],"sourceCredit":"","releasePoint":"119-102","ancestors":[{"type":"title","num":"Title 25—","heading":"INDIANS","identifier":"/us/usc/t25"},{"type":"chapter","num":"CHAPTER 14—","heading":"MISCELLANEOUS","identifier":"/us/usc/t25/ch14"},{"type":"subchapter","num":"SUBCHAPTER XXI—","heading":"NAVAJO AND HOPI TRIBES: REHABILITATION","identifier":"/us/usc/t25/ch14/schXXI"}]}